<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Russian. Follows the same rules the English table states:

   * MODEL AND TIER NAMES and FaceFusion's own option vocabulary stay as they are
     (hyperswap, inswapper, arcface, gpen_bfr_256, v79, "pixel boost"). They are the words
     upstream's documentation uses, and a translated model name is a name nobody can search
     for and nothing can be compared against.
   * The PROCESSOR chips (face_swapper, face_enhancer, lip_syncer) are identifiers, not
     words. Untranslated on purpose, exactly as in Chinese.
   * The LOG and the BUG REPORT are not here at all. They are read by whoever fixes the
     bug, and a translated tier-fallback trace helps no one.
-->
